<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lusici</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lusici were a West Slavic tribe living in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-lusatia">Lower Lusatia</a>, in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and gave the region its name. They were conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gero-the-great">Margrave Gero</a> in 963 and later came under the March of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a>. Together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milceni">Milceni</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-lusatia">Upper Lusatia</a>, they are among the ancestors of the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sorbs">Sorbs</a>.</p></div>
